    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Live agents created with ticked Text IDs. On a language change each agent is refreshed from its current params baseline (so runtime ChangeParams survive): ticked non-structural fields are re-resolved on a clone and only nodes whose text changed are sent. One failed field sends nothing for that agent. An AgentBusy reply marks the agent dirty; the refresh is redone when its turn ends. Applied fires once the latest refresh of an agent is fully acknowledged, or at once when no text changed. A refresh started later makes the replies of an earlier one stale. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
